# better-sqlite3 declares `install: node-gyp rebuild`, but it also ships a
# prebuilt binary for every platform (node_modules/better-sqlite3/prebuilds) and
# loads that at runtime. Running the build script therefore only fails on any
# machine without the Visual Studio C++ toolchain, and succeeds pointlessly on
# the ones that have it. Skipping lifecycle scripts keeps `npm ci` deterministic
# and compiler-free everywhere, including the server, and is a sensible
# supply-chain default.
#
# Verified with this dependency set: next build, eslint and tsx all work.
ignore-scripts=true
